// Title: Regsvr32 Execution From Potential Suspicious Location
// ID: 9525dc73-0327-438c-8c04-13c0e037e9da
// Status: test
// Level: medium
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems), Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-05-26
// Tags: attack.stealth, attack.t1218.010
// Description: Detects execution of regsvr32 where the DLL is located in a potentially suspicious location.
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

process where (((process.command_line like "*_:\\ProgramData\\*" or process.command_line like "*_:\\Temp\\*" or process.command_line like "*_:\\Users\\Public\\*" or process.command_line like "*_:\\Windows\\Temp\\*" or process.command_line like "*_\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\*" or process.command_line like "*_\\AppData\\Roaming\\*")) and ((process.executable endswith "\\regsvr32.exe") or (process.pe.original_file_name == "REGSVR32.EXE")))
